finding: The ingress limits can close a conforming stock client: ReplicationReceiver.flush sends an ACK even on an empty receive after the first confirmation (src/extras/multiplayer/index.ts:671–682), and ClientPrediction calls it from preFixed (prediction.ts:100,251). At 480 render frames/s, the rooms client's fixed-step input sends (examples/rooms/src/network.ts:207–209) add about 60/s to the 480 ACKs/s, exhausting the 3500-token bucket in about 88 s or less, even without operation traffic. Pending operations repeat on every render flush (network.ts:217–218; intent.ts:349–352): a valid near-cap operation repeated across a server drain stall can hit the independent 256 KiB limit in about 65 frames, well before the message budget. The current client encoder also has no packet splitting or corresponding size bound for a batch of pending operations. Neither new check exercises conforming clients under these conditions.
